ilms he had made  before becoming a vod star in the 2010s  and although it made a decent 228  million dollars globally it's hard to  imagine anyone leaving the theater  wanting more still holding the rights to  the character in the early days of the  mcu sony greenlit ghost rider spirit of  vengeance shooting the film largely in  romania and turkey and hoping its cast  of rising stars could take it to the  next level spoiler alert  they didn't spirit of vengeance earned  about half as much as the previous ghost  rider movie and opened to even worse  reviews those factors doomed any chance  of a direct sequel as did sony who lost  the rights to the ghost rider character  in 2013. that same year cage told  collider he was no longer interested in  playing johnny blaze  after laying low for much of the 80s  michael myers returned with 1988's aptly  titled halloween 4 the return of michael  myers kicking off a new trilogy of cheap  slashers that built a ludicrous  backstory for the mute masked serial  killer in short it revolved around his  niece jaime and his unceasing need to  kill everyone who was related to him in  some way all that was retconned out of  existence for 1998's halloween h2o which  jumped back and acted as a direct sequel  to halloween 2. after h2o racked up  nearly 75 million dollars at the box  office another sequel was guaranteed  unfortunately no one bothered to show up  for halloween resurrection which added  buster rhymes to the cast and utilized a  reality tv inspired horror comedy tone  luckily having endured a few more  reboots myers is stronger than ever  these days and has long forgotten  his wayward niece  movie success can be hard to predict and  few could have guessed that a low-key  low-budget fish out of water action  comedy from australia would be the top  grossing comedy of 1986 out earned  globally only by top gun crocodile  dundee starred paul hogan as mick  crocodile dundee a rugged but immensely  charming outdoorsman from the australian  outback who finds himself dealing with a  new way of life in new york city  [Music]  that's a knife just two years later  crocodile dundee ii arrived and it  attracted almost as much box office  business as the previous movie another  sequel would have been warranted but  hogan wanted to try other things for a  while you can thank this era for flipper  after a five-year hiatus from the big  screen hogan was ready to return to what  he thought the people wanted making a  third mcdundee movie crocodile dundee in  los angeles found the character and his  son investigating a possible murder at a  movie studio it took in just 39 million  globally in the summer of 2001 and later  accrued a lowly 11 score on rotten  tomatoes  no matter how implausible it got for  john mclean to keep randomly  encountering bloodthirsty terrorists  hollywood kept churning out die hard  movies the same off-the-wall sequel itis  followed the original speed and for good  reason the hit 1994 action classic after  all was essentially die hard on a bus  but the speed franchise was ultimately  left dead in the water following the  release of speed 2 cruise control keanu  reeves decided not to reprise his role  in the movie so the sequel followed  sandra bullock's annie on a cruise with  her new cop boyfriend alex shaw  portrayed by series newcomer jason  patrick the bad guy the second time  around was a computer hacker played by  willem dafoe but neither the return of  bullock nor defoe's unhinged antics were  enough to create a need for more speed  earning a disappointing 48 million  dollars at the box office in the u.s  speed 2 was seen as one of the more  disappointing high profile releases of  the year nominated for eight razzie  awards it currently holds a shockingly  low four percent at rotten tomatoes  there will likely never be a speed three  and that's not necessarily a bad thing  crease 2 is a classic example of how not  to do a sequel gone from the original  movie word director randall kleiser  stars john travolta and olivia  newton-john and composers jim jacobs and  warren casey the one major thing that  did carry over from greece to greece to  the plot it's almost a complete rehash  except the roles are gender swapped  needless to say grease 2 which came out  four years after the original was not a  huge hit it made 15 million dollars at  the box office about 10 percent of what  greece had earned in the states alone  according to original greece cast member  dede khan who briefly appeared in the  sequel the studio's low expectations for  the first film ultimately doomed greece  too she told tv guide there was a setup  in the first film for a sequel about  summer school but paramount didn't know  greece was going to be such a success so  they passed by the time they got around  to it they couldn't get john anymore so  they came up with a new concept talk of  a third grease occasionally bubbles up  but it always fizzles out eventually  over the course of three movies the  griswolds endured a terrible road trip  to wally world a horrible trip to europe  and a horrible christmas where they  stayed at home by 1997 there was only  one place left to go  vegas  vegas  the fourth film in the vacation series  didn't score with critics or audiences  perhaps because it was the first  vacation movie not to bear the national  lampoon seal of approval or to be at  least partially scripted by john hughes  and despite being set in sin city it's  also the only installment to earn a tame  pg rating vegas vacation took in 36  million at the box office about half of  what christmas vacation had earned  sending the franchise into a long  theatrical deep freeze a few vacation  vets returned for an ill-fated  direct-to-video sequel to christmas  vacation but the family's next big  screen outing wouldn't come until 2015's  vacation original stars chevy chase and  beverly deangelo were relegated to a  cameo for this movie and neither the  reviews nor the box office were enough  to inspire the studio to do much more  with the franchise  2005 sin city was as faithful as a comic  adaptation can get utilizing an  all-digital filming technique robert  rodriguez's film version of the frank  miller series looks like a comic book in  motion perhaps owing in part to the fact  that miller himself has a co-directing  credit dazzling visuals and a noirish  plot led to critical praise and  158 million dollars worldwide making a  sequel more a matter of when than if  despite all that success the filmmakers  took their sweet time getting the next  sin city to the big screen perhaps too  long in fact sin city a dame to kill  fort limped into theaters in 2014 nine  long years after the original long after  most people had moved on by the time a  dame to kill four reached audiences its  once unique visual style had been so  thoroughly absorbed into the mainstream  that it no longer felt fresh or  innovative the movie made just 39  million dollars and suffered a critical  drubbing before it opened rodriguez and  miller said they were already talking  about a third installment but that  chatter has quieted considerably or  maybe they're just taking another decade  between sequels  marvel's fantastic four is one of the  great comic book superhero teams it took  a surprisingly long time for reed  richards and company to make their big  screen debut however and some would  argue they still have it at least not  properly say that again  it's fantastic  yes it is  tapes of a low budget never officially  released 1994 roger corman attempt  became a collector's item while a 100  million dollar fox stab in 2005 grossed  333.5 million dollars and seemed to be  headed in the right direction but the  2007 follow-up fantastic four rise of  the silver server stumbled out of the  gate and never recovered the sequel made  less money than the first movie and its  reviews weren't exactly great either in  2008 star chris evans told mtv news that  the lackluster response to the silver  surfer had effectively killed this take  on the characters he said i've heard  nothing from anyone at fox we had all  planned on doing another one but if  there were going to be a third i think a  week after the second one was released  we would have heard still though hope  lingers on for marvel's first family  here's a formula for box office success  a male character who in desperate times  must dress up in the clothes of an old  woman and then convincingly live as one  until their ruse is discovered robin  williams mrs doubtfire brought in more  than 200 million dollars while martin  lawrence's first two big mama's house  comedies earned a combined 310 million  dollars clearly lots of people found the  idea of lawrence's fbi agent going deep  undercover as a matriarchal southern  woman named big mama to be absolutely  hilarious in 2011 producers found a way  to get lawrence back in drag one more  time while simultaneously attempting to  send the big mama's house franchise in a  new direction in big mamas like father  like son lawrence's character goes  undercover with his stepson trent who  takes on the clothing and guise of a  woman named charmaine it didn't work the  third movie earned far less than its two  predecessors and scored a woeful five  percent on rotten tomatoes those figures  spelled the end for any big mama sequel  starring jackson which he probably  wouldn't want to make anyway he told  comedy hype in 2019 that movie was not  good the whole dress bit was overdone it  was hacky  meet the parents was a rare blockbuster  comedy and one that seemed to announce  ben stiller and robert de niro as the  perfect pairing audiences were left  wanting more and boy was hollywood going  to give it to them i think you've got  some serious issues believe it or not  the 330 million dollar box office hit  was bested by a 522 million dollar  taking for the 2004 sequel meet the  [ __ ] but then little [ __ ] missed  its shot when it arrived in 2010. yes  the film did technically earn 310  million dollars but there's nothing  hollywood likes less in a franchise than  a downward trajectory and the  inexplicably expensive 100 million  dollar price tag didn't help the reviews  were also abysmal and little [ __ ]  became one of the most loathed movies of  the year amassing an embarrassing nine  percent on rotten tomatoes wisely  universal was content to stop the  [ __ ] at three movies  from much of the 80s and into the 90s  the police academy movies seemed harder  to kill than jason voorhees  six films were made between 1984 and  1989 and even roger ebert stuck up for  their existence comparing the franchise  to the bowery boys and abbott and  costello as long as they kept making  money these films kept on coming back  the original film had made 81 million  dollars against a relatively tiny 4.5  million dollar budget police academy 2  their first assignment took in 55.3  million  police academy 3 back in training earned  43 million dollars and so on the pot of  gold was clearly shrinking but as long  as the films were made cheaply they  remained profitable that is until the  seventh film police academy mission to  moscow flopped hard bad luck seemed to  finally catch up with the dim-witted  cadets as the film had a final box  office hall of 126  247  or roughly one percent of its production  budget while critics had gone relatively  easy on the original police academy they  didn't hold back expressing their  distaste for the sequels movies four  through seven all racked up a perfect  zero percent on rotten tomatoes police  academy mission to moscow bombed hard  with audiences and critics alike so hard  that it finally killed an unkillable  franchise  the blade films had everything going for  them years of comic stories to draw from  wesley snipes in his prime and plenty of  kung fu vampire action all the  ingredients were there to keep the  sequel train running but then came blade  trinity the third installment of the  franchise received middling reviews and  disappointing grosses the end result of  an epic collapse that had begun to  unravel even as the cameras were rolling  snipes reportedly engaged in all sorts  of eccentric behavior behind the scenes  including trying to strangle the  director among other things walk by his  trailer and this  wall of of pot stench would just be like  whoa and kind of push you to the side  snipes was so unhappy after the release  of trinity that he ended up suing the  studio while the character is set to  live on in the marvel cinematic universe  blade trinity very much ended snipe  stays as the day walker  it sounds like a hollywood bingo card  reboot a title with ip recognition cast  it with one of the biggest movie stars  on the planet and use it to launch a  shared universe what could possibly go  wrong as it turns out everything hoping  to replicate the success of the mcu  universal announced in 2014 that  filmmakers alex kurtzman and chris  morgan would oversee a series of reboots  of the classic monster movies that had  launched the studio in the 1930s  christened the dark universe universal  very publicly revealed plans for a 2019  bride of frankenstein movie followed by  a new take on frankenstein starring  javier bardem as the monster an  invisible man movie with johnny depp and  a version of dr jekyll and mr hyde  featuring russell crowe in case you  haven't noticed none of these films ever  saw the light of day tom cruise's reboot  of the mummy is to blame for that  audiences had fond associations with the  beloved brendan fraser movies that had  signed off just a decade prior and cruz  still seemed like a box office sure  thing nevertheless the mummy flopped in  every way earning a terrible 16 on  rotten tomatoes and a disappointing 80  million dollars at the domestic box  office in the wake of the failure  kurtzman and morgan abandoned the  franchise followed shortly thereafter by  universal the dark universe had gone out  not with a bang but a whimper  [Music]
 

